198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In response to an extended disruption, global tech companies might seek to diversify their manufacturing bases away from East Asia, particularly from the geopolitical hotbed of Taiwan. This could accelerate efforts to establish semiconductor manufacturing capabilities in regions perceived as more stable, such as the United States and Europe, although replicating TSMC's advanced manufacturing capabilities would be costly and time-consuming. The strategic importance of semiconductor supply might also lead to increased geopolitical tensions and realignments. Countries and regions capable of semiconductor production might find themselves in powerful bargaining positions, while others could become significantly more vulnerable to supply chain disruptions.2)
/Alt ()
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
